{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1237227-help-drowning-in-a-page-of-white-emptiness","id":1237227,"title":"Help! Drowning in a page of white emptiness!!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-20T12:28:16-07:00","id":1237227,"title":"Help! Drowning in a page of white emptiness!!","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> In the near ish future, I will be running a Changeling Game for my group. I have been working for a few months just getting a handle on the basic mechanics of the game. We are all nWoD veterans and will be playing in 1E with some tweaks from Dogs of War. Through sheer stubbornness I taught them MtAw and am now going through the same process with Changeling.<br /> The main issues I\u2019m having at this point are as follows:<br /> Why do they form motley\u2019s? <br /> How do you balance Fae madness in the courts but have it still be an inviting and functional organization? Like I want to put a mad Changeling on one of the thrones to add some delicious tension but it seems like I\ufe0ft would be way to easy to plunge everyone back into Hell.<br /> Are there any further descriptions on the hedge?I understand that it is similar to astral realms but more focused and dangerous. I\u2019m just struggling to grok it. <br /> <br /> One question that my players keep bringing up is what do Changelings do? I have yet to respond with a satisfactory answer for them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also having trouble filling out my freehold at the moment. <br /> Thanks in advanced!<br /> <br /> P.S. I know 2E is on its way, I\u2019m a backer but my group doesn\u2019t want to shift to CofD at this point. Plus I have all the PDFs for 1E<br /> <br /> P.P.S. I posted this from mobile, please forgive any glaring errors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3905,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3905-llewyd42","user":"Llewyd42","date":". 07-20-2018, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3905-llewyd42","name":"Llewyd42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:20:07-07:00","id":1237269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Llewyd42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1237227-help-drowning-in-a-page-of-white-emptiness#post1237227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S. I know 2E is on its way, I\u2019m a backer but my group doesn\u2019t want to shift to CofD at this point. Plus I have all the PDFs for 1E</div> </div> </div> </div>But... the mechanics are so much <i>better</i>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Llewyd42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1237227-help-drowning-in-a-page-of-white-emptiness#post1237227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they form motley\u2019s?</div> </div> </div> </div>Support group. Both mentally, and because coming back from a Durance, alone, is a dangerous place to be. Friends can look after each other, even if it just to make sure you aren't talking to the teapots and planning to bake kinder pie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Llewyd42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1237227-help-drowning-in-a-page-of-white-emptiness#post1237227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you balance Fae madness in the courts but have it still be an inviting and functional organization? Like I want to put a mad Changeling on one of the thrones to add some delicious tension but it seems like I\ufe0ft would be way to easy to plunge everyone back into Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Courts have organization, and organizations have resources. Proprietary magic too. Even with a crackpot at the helm, there is opportunity is large organizations (for instance, have you seen USA politics lately?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Llewyd42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1237227-help-drowning-in-a-page-of-white-emptiness#post1237227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any further descriptions on the hedge?I understand that it is similar to astral realms but more focused and dangerous. I\u2019m just struggling to grok it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of those magic forests in books, but applied to the general surroundings. The local topographic become like a fairy-tale, except with more barbed wire encouraging you to <i>stay-the-F-on-the-path</i>. The alleys loom extra-creepy. Think of it as if a cartoon character were viewing a spooky place and exaggerating the dangers (and wonders, too - the Hedge isn't all bad). It's familiar, but clearly <i>not normal</i>. Oh, and Trolls will break your legs if you don't pay the toll to cross their bridge. Maintenance fees, you know?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Llewyd42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1237227-help-drowning-in-a-page-of-white-emptiness#post1237227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question that my players keep bringing up is what do Changelings do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pick up the pieces.<br /> <br /> More seriously, the PCs just came back from hell to find that the world moved on without them, and that they've <i>changed</i>. Oh, and hell wants them back (whenever it gets around to it). So, they could:<ul><li>Try to reclaim their old life (problems with that, though).</li> <li>Carve out a new place for themselves.</li> <li>Try to get their mind back together and establish a sense of peace.</li> <li>Make sure they never get dragged back their again.</li> <li>Make sure no one <i>else</i> they can about gets dragged there to begin with.</li> <li>Deal with the inevitable shit that happens, and that they need to deal with, even if it may not concern them, because <i>someone</i> has to.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:29:05-07:00","id":1237273,"title":"","content":"Think of motelys as close-knit support groups. Changelings might form them because they all escaped from the same Keeper, because they all returned to Earth around the same time, to pursue a shared goal, because the Wyrd keeps drawing them together, etc. It's nice to have a group of people who've mystically promised not to betray you that you can talk about your problems with.<br /> <br /> The thing with changeling society is that everyone is at least a little traumatized, exposed to experiences beyond human ken, and so compassion becomes a double-edged sword. A lot of questionable behaviors, especially those that aren't outright destructive, might get excused or overlooked because you understand that your fellow courtiers are still coping with some terrible things that have happened to them. The combination of Wyrd and Clarity also means the changleings may often second-guess their perceptions of others: Maybe she's acting strangely because of a Frailty or to fulfill an Oath, or maybe you're projecting your own Durance onto her actions. Plus, she's contributed so much to the Court, other changelings depend on her; do you really want to take all the good she's done away from everyone just because of some eccentricity? I think that's the kind of attitude that allows Fae behavior to metastasize in a Court. <br /> <br /> <i>Rites of Spring, Autumn Nightmares</i>, and <i>Dancers in the Dusk</i> all expand on the Hedge. That last book provides a bunch of example locations that might exist within the Thorns; it's very evocative.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking changelings are trying to figure out their place in a world from which they were stolen, when going back to their old lives usually isn't an option. They have to balance mortal concerns with the lure of Faerie. In 1st edition, note that extended isolation from humans risks Clarity loss; that alone can at least provide the beginnings of a motivation for doing something. Furthermore, changelings have had their eyes opened to the fact that there are incredibly powerful, solipsistic aliens who love to take people and turn them into playthings somewhere out there in the wild yonder. That can also be a powerful impetus for action.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T18:28:12-07:00","id":1248911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Llewyd42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1237227-help-drowning-in-a-page-of-white-emptiness#post1237227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all,<br /> <br /> Through sheer stubbornness I taught them MtAw and am now going through the same process with Changeling.<br /> The main issues I\u2019m having at this point are as follows:<br /> Why do they form motley\u2019s?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that you are setting your Changeling campaign in the same town or city were you set your mage campaign the changelings may be responding to the mages actions. For example if the mages actions prompted the local vampire community to hunt down and kill the other supernaturals in town the changelings may be banding together for protection. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T07:06:49-07:00","id":1249956,"title":"","content":"Haha no the Mage game was basically National Treasure crosses with Oceans 11 as an avatar of revolution was rising from the Temenos and they need the document for the binding. What I\u2019m trying to say is it was a short series and not meant to be interconnected.<br /> <br /> Right now they are clamoring for a Dresden Files Fae adventure in chicago. So I\u2019m starting to reread Summer Knight, Small Favor, and cold days to pick up inspiration. So far I\u2019m going to split the seasonal courts into seelie and unseelie alliances. Trying to figure out what to flavor the Gentry in the local area Arcadian side. <br /> My players have started working on their characters and so far:<br /> A Spring Fairest Dual kithed snowskin/<br /> A Spring Wizened Dual kithed Smith/Telluric faerie astronaut<br /> An Autumn Darkling undecided<br /> An Autumn Darkling or beast undecided <br /> A Winter Fairest twin to the spring fairest<br /> <br /> They have mentioned interest in exploring the hedge and cultivating goblinfruits. I haven\u2019t really brought up hollows but was going to introduce them with various community hollows if he freehold and courts.<br /> <br /> I appreciate all the feed back. I still don\u2019t get how you would naturally get cross court motley\u2019s. But I get Motley\u2019s are you friends your cliche whereas your court is your scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3905-llewyd42","name":"Llewyd42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T14:08:03-07:00","id":1250059,"title":"","content":"While there is natural overlap of interests with intra-Court Motleys, inter-Court Motleys offer broader capabilities, multiple niches, and can act as bonding agents for potentially fractious politics. And, as you said, your friends are your friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T16:03:19-07:00","id":1250558,"title":"","content":"I think I've read most of the Dresden files but my lore on Chicago is limited. I believe it was captured by the British during the war of 1812 and I think someone named Chrysler was beaten up by a Clurichaun known locally as The Red Dwarf. According to Frank Joseph in his book &quot;Lost Colonies of Ancient America&quot; the Waubansee stone now in the basement on the Chicago Historical Society was originally a Tophet used by Phoenician priests for infant sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, there was also that episode of Monster Quest about the Dogman. There is a music video on YouTube to go with a song The Dogman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","user":"moonwolf8","date":". 09-01-2018, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}